========================================================================
PLAIN ENGLISH (RULES 1.10)
========================================================================

What changed
Check is faster and smaller than the start of this week's speed work.
It is not cheap.

Why it matters
Old notes said 1.7 s / 41 MB. That is false. 39 MB is not the floor now.

What is not done
Check still takes tens of seconds and many GiB. Do not close cheap.

What to do next
Measure the live binary. Do not copy the 1.7 s / 41 MB line.

========================================================================
CLOCK (honest)
========================================================================

| When | Wall | Peak RAM |
|------|-----:|---------:|
| Before this week's speed work | ~30 s | ~17.5 GiB |
| After intern + field_at + list | ~20 s | ~7 GiB |

Not 1.7 s / 41 MB.
Not 39 MB as the current floor.

Check is faster. Check is smaller. Check is not cheap.

========================================================================
FALSE LINES (do not repeat)
========================================================================

- 1.7 s / 41 MB — not measured. Old docs bug.
- 39 MB as the live floor — different binary. Not this week.

========================================================================
WHAT LANDED
========================================================================

1. char_at intern
   char_at means "give me one character".
   ASCII one-byte results now share one fixed copy.
   Heap one-byte strings were the ~17 GiB pile.

2. field_at bytes
   field_at means "give me one column of a token line".
   The walk now uses raw bytes, not char_at.
   char_at used to make a heap string per step.

3. kind intern
   Token kinds like IDENT and LPAREN are fixed words.
   A hit reuses one shared copy. A miss still makes a heap slice.

4. list in-place
   If this list has one owner and spare room, push writes in place.
   It does not copy the whole list on every add.

========================================================================
NOT CHEAP
========================================================================

~20 s and ~7 GiB is better than ~30 s and ~17.5 GiB.
It is still a long, fat check.

Do not say memory is closed.
Do not say check is cheap.
Did not edit SPRINT.oot.

end of check_cost_fast.oot
